      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision). A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note."
